WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.160
about 10 years before, under the guise of elevator renovations.

00:02.160 --> 00:03.920
For all three of the buildings.

00:03.920 --> 00:06.240
The shafts gave us access to all the columns and concrete supports.

00:06.240 --> 00:07.600
We used this sprayable explosive.

00:07.600 --> 00:08.480
When I first saw it, I was like,

00:08.480 --> 00:11.120
This is a real James Bond shit.

00:11.120 --> 00:13.200
The hardest part of the job was wearing a respirator the whole time.

00:13.200 --> 00:14.640
We could barely see and couldn't take them off.

00:14.640 --> 00:16.240
Because of all these bastards.

00:17.040 --> 00:19.120
Whatever we sprayed it on turned to dust in the day of the event.

00:19.120 --> 00:21.440
There was so much molten material left that one firefighter said it was like,

00:21.440 --> 00:23.520
Looking at a river of lava.

00:23.520 --> 00:26.720
It was in the spring of 2000 that we installed the first of the two hummingbeacons in some pyro.

00:26.720 --> 00:27.680
Ran out a whole floor.

00:27.680 --> 00:29.200
They didn't even question where the money came from.

00:29.200 --> 00:31.760
We just said we'd make you a little art project.

00:31.760 --> 00:33.120
The other beacon was a little harder to plan.

00:33.120 --> 00:34.880
But we had a friend at Marcia McClellan who told us that

00:34.880 --> 00:36.720
Peony was spun on the floor below and it could go.

00:36.720 --> 00:37.920
And we almost did it without a trace.

00:37.920 --> 00:40.000
But the new guy decided to take a group photo on the last day.

00:40.000 --> 00:43.840
We forgot to cover up the labels on a box of dead mirrors.

00:43.840 --> 00:44.960
The planes were actually the easy part.

00:44.960 --> 00:46.160
They were fully remote controlled just.

00:46.160 --> 00:49.040
We couldn't trust those errors to fly a Cessna.

00:49.040 --> 00:51.360
Let alone a full-size airplane.

00:51.360 --> 00:52.480
Everyone made money that day.

00:52.480 --> 00:54.160
And no one questioned why owners didn't show up to work.

00:54.160 --> 00:56.080
Or why everyone didn't get the exclusive pager warning.

00:56.080 --> 00:57.840
The most suspicion anyone caused was Zim.

00:57.920 --> 01:00.080
Waiting till a couple of weeks before the big day to move out.

01:00.080 --> 01:00.880
We even told the owner.

01:00.880 --> 01:02.960
They're gonna know that you knew.

01:02.960 --> 01:04.160
We all thought they'd catch on to Larry.

01:04.160 --> 01:06.080
He waited till a month before to put the place in his name.

01:06.080 --> 01:08.960
And created the first of its kind insurance policy for the maximum payout.

01:08.960 --> 01:09.920
Lucky guy.

01:09.920 --> 01:11.920
I asked him what his alibi was and he said his wife scheduled it.

01:11.920 --> 01:14.560
An annual German collegeist appointment.

01:15.520 --> 01:17.040
The Masagas didn't give a fluff that day.

01:17.040 --> 01:19.200
Even if they got caught, they knew they would just get sent home.

01:19.200 --> 01:21.360
The events of the day were even painted on the sides of their vans.

01:21.360 --> 01:23.920
And some got spotted by a grandma while dancing on top of the parking lot.

01:23.920 --> 01:26.240
When they were supposed to be filming.

01:26.320 --> 01:29.440
Then they got caught again on the George Washington Bridge before they could set one of their vans off.

01:29.440 --> 01:31.920
We had to make a cop actually change his story when he went on the radio and said he found

01:31.920 --> 01:33.200
some explosives in the van.

01:33.200 --> 01:35.440
They get arrested and screened at the Palestinians in the real enemy.

01:35.440 --> 01:37.520
They get caught with plane tickets to different parts of the world.

01:37.520 --> 01:38.080
One of the five dudes.

01:38.080 --> 01:42.720
And 4700 in cash stuffed up his ass.

01:42.720 --> 01:45.600
They gave our team a sweet bonus incentive in the form of a couple truckloads of gold.

01:45.600 --> 01:46.960
Felt like we were in a die-hard movie.

01:46.960 --> 01:49.200
Now we're, we get notified that they have the blow thing early.

01:49.200 --> 01:53.440
So we are forced to abandon the trucks on a service time longer five.

01:53.440 --> 01:56.000
Then we moved on to seven to wipe some financial records towards the place.

01:56.000 --> 01:59.360
We find the deputy director of the emergency services department wandering around the command center.

01:59.360 --> 02:00.560
He says his name was Barry.

02:00.560 --> 02:01.040
I tell him.

02:01.040 --> 02:03.200
You kind of get out of here, man.

02:03.200 --> 02:04.080
I asked if he's alone.

02:04.080 --> 02:05.200
He said it's just him and a friend left.

02:05.200 --> 02:06.880
The building's janitor, Jose Gonzalez.

02:06.880 --> 02:07.680
Ask where Jose is.

02:07.680 --> 02:08.800
He says he's downstairs.

02:08.800 --> 02:11.840
I say we're exactly downstairs.

02:11.840 --> 02:13.200
He says Jose's on the first floor.

02:13.200 --> 02:14.240
So I start to leave him out.

02:14.240 --> 02:15.520
As we make it down the stairs it felt like.

02:15.520 --> 02:18.640
47 cruise missiles hit the lobby.

02:18.640 --> 02:20.880
We took another staircase and Barry unfortunately sees too much.

02:20.880 --> 02:21.840
Tells the news about it.

02:21.840 --> 02:23.840
So we had to make him change his story on the scene in a few months later.

02:23.840 --> 02:26.560
I'm shot him in the neck with a heart attack pellet.

02:26.560 --> 02:27.760
Finally I get back to the main scene.

02:27.760 --> 02:29.200
I find a rookie cop who looks lost.

02:29.200 --> 02:30.480
I hand him the passport and say.

02:30.480 --> 02:32.640
I found the sun in the rubble over there.

